Start here: You do not need to know programming before learning Git. Git is simply a tool that
remembers changes made to files.
Before Git: the common problem
Imagine you are writing a school report. You save many copies:
report.docx
report-final.docx
report-final-2.docx
report-final-really-final.docx
After some time, you may not know which copy is correct. You may also delete good work by mistake. If
several people edit the same project, the confusion becomes worse.
Git solves this problem by keeping an organized history of the project. Instead of making many confusing
copies, you keep one project and ask Git to record important moments.
The simplest definition
Git is a tool that tracks changes in files and lets you save named checkpoints.
